 "entryNodeId": "bottom-panel",
 "rationale": "A flat-pack crate is separate boards by definition and its 460 mm panels are far past any print bed, so it splits into four CNC-routed plywood designs: one side panel placed twice (mirrored by rotation), the floor, a plain slat placed four times and a hand-hold slat placed twice. Each slat joint carries two screws per end, so the 12 declared joints across two panel copies mint the 24 countersunk slat screws, and the two floor joints mint the four long screws.",
 "design": "Honest flat-pack woodwork: square-cut plywood boards with lightly eased (about 1 mm round-over) outside edges, no decoration, proportions that read as a sturdy utility crate. Countersunk heads sit flush on the outside faces; the hand-hold is a generously rounded stadium with fully rounded edges for comfort.",
